{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And they shall eat the flesh</b> The verse begins with eating and ends with eating — על מרורים יאכלוהו — hinting that two eatings are required: the eating of the Paschal offering and the eating of the festival offering:" "<b>They shall eat it</b> And adjacent to it is אל תאכלו — to say that they shall eat it specifically for the sake of Pesach and not for coarse eating:" "<b>יאכלוהו</b> Four times in the Masorah: two in matters of Pesach, and the other two — אהרן ובניו יאכלוהו in the matter of the ordination. Just as there they were commanded ומפתח אוהל מועד לא תצאו, here too ואתם לא תצאו איש מפתח ביתו. And the other — כי מאספיו יאכלוהו — for the final redemption is juxtaposed to the first redemption:"], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {2 "The fourth occurrence, כי מאספיו יאכלוהו, is unaddressed by the author; it is Exodus 29:33."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:34.086071168Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}